WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.227 --> 00:00:13.354
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The best thing about the weather in London is that it’s hardly ever extreme.

2
00:00:13.631 --> 00:00:17.449
It isn’t usually very hot or very cold.

3
00:00:19.149 --> 00:00:27.502
In summer, it’s sometimes sunny and sometimes cloudy, with temperatures of about 22 degrees.

4
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:32.214
And of course, it sometimes rains.

5
00:00:34.192 --> 00:00:40.415
In winter, the temperature is usually between zero and ten degrees.

6
00:00:42.078 --> 00:00:47.647
It can be windy and cold, but it hardly ever snows.

7
00:00:48.907 --> 00:00:58.204
In spring and in autumn the weather is very changeable – you can have all four seasons in one day!

8
00:00:58.506 --> 00:01:04.100
It can be sunny in the morning, cloudy at lunchtime,

9
00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:10.198
raining in the afternoon, and then cold and windy in the evening.

10
00:01:10.424 --> 00:01:17.580
It’s a good idea for tourists to take their sunglasses and their umbrellas when they go out.

11
00:01:17.983 --> 00:01:23.980
One thing you don’t often see these days in London is fog.

12
00:01:24.446 --> 00:01:27.634
A lot of tourists come to London and say,

13
00:01:27.684 --> 00:01:31.778
‘Where’s the fog? London is always foggy in films!’

14
00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:38.531
Well, it’s true that in the past, that is until the 1950s,

15
00:01:38.645 --> 00:01:43.835
London was a very foggy city because the air was really dirty.

16
00:01:44.251 --> 00:01:50.374
But today the air is quite clean and it’s hardly ever foggy.